 seen what he looked like in  Tarzan the way he got in shape and the  way he buffed up you can see that he  would make a pretty dang good Sentry he  even has the long blonde hair in that  movie so I honestly think that either of  these two actors would make a pretty  dang good Sentry and I like both of them  for this choice I think each would bring  something different to the table but  each would do a really good job and both  of them are able to bulk up and be  really really big for the role because  like everybody is calling him he is  essentially Marvel Superman so naturally  and kind of unfortunately I think people  are going to compare Century to Henry  Cavill Superman so whoever plays role is  gonna have to get jacked now as far as  Sentry being the villain in the  Thunderbolts film I think I pretty much  know how this is going to work now first  things first you have to know that it is  confirmed that Harrison Ford is going to  be replacing William Hurt as Thunderbolt  Ross sadly William Hurt passed away but  Marvel Studios had some pretty big plans  for his character Thunderbolt Ross so  they have decided to recast and Harrison  Ford is confirmed it has also been  reported that Thunderbolt Ross is going  to be the president in the Thunderbolts  movie the president of the United States  and on top of that it is confirmed that  we are going to see him turn into Red  Hulk in the movie actually what is kind  of interesting is all of this is  confirmed for Captain America 4 New  World Order which will come out only  months before the Thunderbolts film so  so Captain America 4 is going to set up  a lot of events of the Thunderbolts  specifically concerning the super  soldier serum which has a direct  involvement with Sentry as well now  Robert Reynolds AKA Sentry was a meth  addict he was a meth head and one day he  broke into a laboratory where he  discovered the golden Century serum and  he consumed it now the golden Century  serum was essentially the super soldier  serum but magnified by about a hundred  thousand so think about how strong  Captain America was and magnify that by  a ton now what had happened was was in  1947 Canada's Department K and the  United States operation rebirth pulled  their resources to become project Sentry  and attempted to recreate the super  soldier serum but not just recreate it  but magnify its effects by one hundred  thousand unfortunately 30 years into  this this project had turned into about  a thousand different subunits and they  didn't really have any type of system in  place to monitor all of these subunits  so basically every unit was kind of just  doing whatever they felt like with no  real regulation whatsoever so you have  all of these sub units trying to  recreate the super soldier serum except  a hundred times more powerful so Robert  Reynolds breaks into one of the labs and  consumes the golden Century serum giving  him the power of a million exploding  Suns when he consumed this he killed his  partner and all of the lab's guards but  obviously he loved the effect and he  asked the professor to make him more  however the project leaders discovered  what happened and they were appalled  appalled at what had happened but also  appalled that they didn't really have  any system in place to make sure that  stuff like this didn't happen so they  asked Robert Reynolds if they could do  tests on him in which he agreed but soon  they couldn't really control him as his  desire to do good by his powers was too  much so he finally left he sewed himself  a costume and called himself Sentry and  from there on century was a hero like I  said he became friends with a lot of  different superheroes and Spider-Man  even looked up to him after Century  discovered his identity was Peter Parker  but unfortunately What followed is what  I think is going to possibly show up in  the Thunderbolts a being called the void  arrived which was a shadowy monster  which essentially used a person's own  greatest fears against them and it  murdered over one million people in  Manhattan however it was discovered that  the void was the own dark aspect of  Sentry's own powers so the only way to  beat the void was to team up with Reed  Richards and Doctor Strange to create a  system which made Earth's entire  population forget that Century ever  existed sounds kind of familiar doesn't  it Doctor Strange was even involved in  that as well making everybody forget  that Peter Parker existed in that he was  Spider-Man but in the story when  everybody forgot that century and Robert  Reynolds existed the void vanished the  void was powered by the Century's Powers  but here's where things get really  interesting eventually Robert Reynolds  was captured and he was brought to the  mutant Illusionist Mastermind and he  implanted a mental virus inside of  Century's mind basically telling him and  convincing him that if he used his  powers a devil would appear this  prevented him from using his powers so  I'm assuming something like this is  going to happen in the Thunderbolts  Robert Reynolds will most likely be the  subject of some super soldier experiment  with an amplified super soldier serum it  will most likely be successful for him  turning him into Century however the  government is probably going to implant  something inside of his head that  basically makes him work for them  however he might get too much out of  control or an actual villain might take  control over him and that is why he is  going to be a villain however he is  going to be the product of some United  States experiment so the United States  has to take care of it so it doesn't get  out so that is why they send the  Thunderbolts team because it's kind of a  sketchy experiment and you probably  don't want people to know about it so  you send the Thunderbolts team the group  of villains and we all know Thunderbolt  Ross has been searching for super  soldier serum and most likely  experimenting on it for a while so this  is most likely a byproduct of his  experiment so that is why he is going to  be involved as well and how we'll most  likely see Red Hulk but I'm assuming by  the end of the Thunderbolts film or  maybe even in the post-credits scene for  it we will see Century become good be  released from whatever mental prison  he's being put under whether that's a  mental microchip or an illusion or  hypnosis that will be released and  Century should be a hero in the MCU and  I'm really excited for it but hey let me  know what you think about this in the  comments down below and does this make  you excited for the Thunderbolts let me  know down below don't forget to like the  video and subscribe so you don't miss  out on any of the latest news for live  updates you can follow me on Instagram  and Twitter and as always thank you all  so much for watching woof woof
 

